From Canvas:
"Problem Description
In this project [our] team will:
[1.] Generate all possible permutations of small integer arrays.
[2.] Run multiple sorting algorithms on each permutation.
[3.] Count the number of comparisons each algorithm makes.
[4.] Identify the best 10, worst 10, and average performances.
[5.] Use the collected data to make and defend Big-O / Big-Ω / Big-Θ style estimates based on your measurements.
[NOTE:] For this project [we] will specifically compare mergesort, quicksort, shaker sort (a bidirectional bubble sort), and heapsort[...]
...You may use textbook or online versions of these algorithms as long as you (a) understand them, (b) clearly comment them, and (c) document your source."
